cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Notes from a Lean formalization of Navier-Stokes local regularity theory:
  claim scope, an independent audit, a methods note, and one open statement
type: software
message: >-
  If you refer to these notes, please cite them as below. Note the claim scope:
  this work does not prove epsilon-regularity, partial regularity, or anything
  bearing on the Clay Millennium Prize problem.
authors:
  - family-names: "Li"
    given-names: "Wei-Ting"
    alias: "bally65"
    affiliation: "Chaoyang University of Technology, Taichung, Taiwan"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-8891-330X"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22684542"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-10"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/bally65/navier-stokes-lean-notes"
abstract: >-
  Four documents from an ongoing Lean 4 / mathlib formalization of local
  regularity theory for the three-dimensional incompressible Navier-Stokes
  equations. They comprise a claim scope, an independent audit of a third
  party's public formalization, a methods note on gating machine-generated Lean
  proofs, and one open Lean statement on which help is sought. The
  formalization itself is not included.
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - mathlib
  - Navier-Stokes equations
  - partial regularity
  - formal verification
  - reproducibility
